## Summary
On the **Windows** desktop app (v0.15.1), the standard zoom shortcuts `Ctrl +`, `Ctrl -`, and `Ctrl 0` do nothing. There is no way to change UI/text size from the keyboard, and no in-app font-size control to fall back on (Settings → Appearance only offers Color Mode / Theme / Tool Call Display).

## Environment
- App version: **0.15.1**
- OS: **Windows 11** (frameless build, `titleBarStyle: 'hidden'`)

## Root cause
In `apps/desktop/electron/main.cjs`, the application menu — the only thing carrying the zoom accelerators — is disabled on every non-mac platform:

```js
// app.whenReady()  (~line 4100)
if (IS_MAC) {
  Menu.setApplicationMenu(buildApplicationMenu())
} else {
  Menu.setApplicationMenu(null)   // Windows/Linux: no menu ⇒ no zoom accelerators
}
```

`buildApplicationMenu()` is where the zoom roles live (`{ role: 'resetZoom' }`, `{ role: 'zoomIn' }`, `{ role: 'zoomOut' }`, ~line 2734). With the menu `null` on Windows/Linux, Electron never registers those role accelerators, so `Ctrl +/-/0` are unbound.

The existing `before-input-event` handlers do **not** cover zoom — they only handle DevTools (`F12` / `Ctrl+Shift+I`, `installDevToolsShortcut` ~line 2769) and preview-close (`Ctrl+W`, `installPreviewShortcut` ~line 2783). So there is no fallback once the menu is gone.

Note: with `setApplicationMenu(null)` on Windows, the `reload`/`forceReload` roles are also unbound, so `Ctrl+R` doesn't refresh either.

## Suggested fix
Add a zoom handler that works regardless of menu state, mirroring the existing shortcut helpers:

```js
function installZoomShortcuts(window) {
  const wc = window.webContents
  wc.on('before-input-event', (event, input) => {
    const mod = IS_MAC ? input.meta : input.control
    if (!mod || input.alt) return
    const key = input.key
    if (key === '=' || key === '+' || key === 'Add') {
      event.preventDefault(); wc.setZoomFactor(Math.min(3, wc.getZoomFactor() + 0.1))
    } else if (key === '-' || key === 'Subtract') {
      event.preventDefault(); wc.setZoomFactor(Math.max(0.5, wc.getZoomFactor() - 0.1))
    } else if (key === '0') {
      event.preventDefault(); wc.setZoomFactor(1)
    }
  })
}
```

Alternatively, register a minimal hidden menu containing the zoom (and reload) roles on non-mac so the accelerators bind.
